#: ../chapter03.rst:337
msgid "TEAM FOLDERS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:339
msgid "The idea of a Team Folder is similar to that of a local network share. Users can be assigned to a Team Folder with read and write permissions at the share level. Inside the folder, at the sub-folder level, each sub-folder can define its own folder level permissions."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:342
msgid "Add a Team Folder"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:347
msgid "CREATING A TEAM FOLDER"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:349
msgid "In the hosted |prodname| environment, you can create Team Folders in several different ways."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:352
msgid "Default Storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:352
msgid "Create a new Team Folder from scratch using the default storage. It will be empty to start with and you can put files and folders inside later."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:355
msgid "Existing Folder(s)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:355
msgid "Create a new folder by selecting one or more existing folders. Those selected folders will show up inside the Team Folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:358
msgid "Publish Tenant Home Storage As a Team Folder"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:358
msgid "The tenant's home storage will be published to users in the same tenant so they can see file and folder contents from the home storage. Some specialized folders such as folders from remote file servers or remote cloud storage services are not included in this scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:362
msgid "Remote File Server (with Server Agent)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:361
msgid "Once you install the Server Agent on your remote server, you can create a Team Folder here."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:364
msgid "Initially without remote Server Agent installed, the Remote server section is empty. If there is at least one Server Agent installed, the remote file server will show up under the \"Remote File Servers\" section and you will be able to import file servers from a remote location, together with Active Directory Identities and the corresponding folder level NTFS permissions."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:369
msgid "TEAM FOLDER SETTINGS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:377
msgid "REPORTS > SHARED OBJECTS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:379
msgid "In |prodname|, you can share files and folders from your file browser. Once a something has been shared it will show up in the Shared Objects view of the Reports section of the portal. The shares can be read-only or full access, and can be controlled by date or shared as a public link. This is how Guest Users are created in |prodname|."
msgstr ""

